  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: The RNA encoder is the largest single performance lever identified so far (pca_n2000→scvi_n200 in multiprofile/avgpool: 0.591→0.650, ~6 pp). scgpt is the only encoder completely untested. Question: config_008 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) is a clean one-variable comparison against config_005 (same settings, scvi_n200, acc 0.650), isolating the effect of the RNA encoder while holding profile, aggregation, and modality constant. Why this is the best next experiment: Before investing budget in multimodal fusion (where the image signal is very weak at 0.208) or new image encoders, we should first establish the ceiling of the RNA encoder landscape. If scgpt outperforms scvi_n200, it reshapes the entire search strategy; if it underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 as the best encoder and can confidently build multimodal experiments on top of it. This single experiment reduces the most critical remaining uncertainty about representation quality at minimal cost."
}

